1
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:58,500
Merry Madagascar is a animation, family film directed by David Soren.

2
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:51,000
While trapped on the island of Madagascar, the Central Park Zoo escapees receive a visit
from Santa--crash landing on their territory and getting amnesia to boot!

3
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:43,500
The animals must help Santa assume his rightful place in the universe,
while King Julian laps up the opportunity for his subjects.

4
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Alex (voice), played by Ben Stiller.

5
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:28,500
Marty (voice), played by Chris Rock.

6
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Melman (voice), played by David Schwimmer.

7
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:13,500
Gloria (voice), played by Jada Pinkett Smith.

8
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Maurice (voice), played by Cedric the Entertainer.

9
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:58,500
Mort (voice), played by Andy Richter.

10
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Merry Madagascar is a Christmas special that was first broadcast on the NBC network on November 17, 2009, which starred
the characters from the film series Madagascar, and takes place sometime between the first and second film.

11
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:43,500
It is the second DreamWorks Animation Christmas special, after Shrek the Halls.

12
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
It features many of the same voices from the film, including Ben
Stiller, Chris Rock, David Schwimmer, and Jada Pinkett Smith.

13
00:24:22,500 --> 00:24:28,500
The only major exception was Sacha Baron Cohen as King Julien XIII, who was replaced by Danny
Jacobs, who also voices the character on The Penguins of Madagascar TV series.

14
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Carl Reiner provided the voice of Santa Claus.

15
00:28:07,500 --> 00:28:13,500
The film explores themes of amnesia, holiday, lion, hippopotamus, giraffe.
